      "provenance": "official-history",
      "originalText": "The calculation of the food income from garrisoned herdable animals now uses a non-linear calculation, where garrisoning additional herdable animals has diminishing returns. 15 \\*(ln FoodAmount/200+1), where FoodAmount is the sum of food in all garrisoned herdable animals. This means garrisoning more herdables will have diminishing returns. Garrisoning all of a player’s own herdables on a map with standard resources (like Arabia) now grants ~15% less food income than before.",
